  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new module `camcraft_tools::meridian` adds the tool meridian. The meridian is the cutting outline `rho(z)` of a mill, tip up. It is made of lines and circular arcs.\n- `Meridian` uses the `SpunPoint` form (`z`, `r`, signed `arc`). It holds one cutting flag for each segment. A pilot bearing band is a non-cutting segment.\n- `Tool::meridian()` gives the meridian of these kinds: `EndMill`, `BallNose`, `BullNose`, `Drill`, `Taper`, `TSlot`, `Keyseat`, `Dovetail`, `Lollipop`.\n- `Meridian::atoms(bound, sag)` splits the meridian into convex solids of revolution:\n  - a line gives a frustum;\n  - an arc that bulges away from the axis gives a torus zone;\n  - an arc that bulges toward the axis gives chord frusta (`Bound::Outer`) or tangent frusta (`Bound::Inner`). Each part stays within the sag limit.\n- Each atom carries the cutting flag of its segment.\n- Degenerate input gives a named `MeridianError`. It never panics.\n- No consumer reads the meridian yet. No toolpath, simulation, check or posted output changes.\n\n## Latest review fixes\n\n- Validate the shape dimensions before a calculation or a fallback. Preserve the named errors `NonFinite`, `Negative` and `Short`.\n- Normalize the line interpolation before multiplication. The accepted `1e308`-height line returns the correct midpoint radius, `5.5`.\n- Reject non-finite segment lengths and unsupported circle coordinates with `OutOfRange`. The documented arc bound is `MAX_ARC_COORD = 1e150`. This bound keeps squared circle terms finite.\n- Calculate each circle midpoint from its start and half its delta. This avoids overflow in endpoint sums.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is sub-issue 1 of #3351 (option C, the hybrid shape model). The maintainer asked for tapered and router tooling. Later sub-issues make the consumers read the tool shape through this meridian.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `verify::probe_meridian_tests::meridian_atoms_match_cutter_atoms_for_each_mill_kind` (camcraft-sim lib). For 12 tools of each listed kind, the meridian atoms are the solids that `Cutter::atoms` builds today. The test compares `z0`, `z1` and `rho` at 65 heights, within 1e-9 mm. The cases include a ball and a bull nose shorter than the corner, and a cone taller than the flute.\n- `meridian::tests::meridian_agrees_with_profile_on_the_cutting_band` (camcraft-tools lib). The meridian agrees with `Tool::profile` at each profile vertex on the cutting band.\n- `meridian::tests::concave_arc_outer_bound_contains_and_inner_bound_stays_inside`. For sag limits 0.1, 0.01 and 0.001 mm: the outer union contains the arc, the inner union stays inside it, and each sag is under the limit. The bearing band is the one non-cutting atom.\n- `meridian::tests::degenerate_meridians_are_refused_by_name`: too few points, zero-length segment, negative radius, non-finite value, arc tighter than its chord, segment that runs back, arc that folds, concave arc through the axis, flag count, bad sag limit, sag limit too fine.\n- `meridian::tests::tool_meridian_refuses_bad_tools_by_name`: a kind that is not a mill, NaN, negative and zero diameter, a bull corner over half the diameter, a dovetail that `undercut::refusal` names.\n\nRed before the change: the sim pin did not compile (`E0432: unresolved import camcraft_tools::meridian`, `E0599: no method named meridian`).\n\nThe first green run found float dust: `bull: rho(0) 3.0000000298023224 vs 3`. A centre error of 1e-16 gives 3e-8 mm of error at the z extreme of the circle. The fix snaps the centre when an arc end sits at the centre's radius.\n\nMutation checks (each red, then restored and green):\n\n- fold guard removed: `degenerate_meridians_are_refused_by_name` red (`Ok(..)` vs `Err(ArcFolds(1))`).\n- through-axis guard removed: the same test red (`Ok(..)` vs `Err(Negative(1))`).\n- outer and inner bounds swapped: `concave_arc_outer_bound_contains_and_inner_bound_stays_inside` red (`outer under the arc at z 4.01`).\n- centre snap absent: the sim pin red (`bull: rho(0) 3.0000000298023224 vs 3`).\n\nFinal validation for this fix round:\n\n- Head: `0948d7989ab0b8e217dd99193da23acf4a880586`. The gates started with base `74ea8988d800f00d41547ec9d292077d2bc3ddc5`.\n- `upstream/main` advanced during the heavy run to `60376ccbbfa52305db6fa880278222e7854fcdbf`. Both bases have the same merge base and the same three-dot diff. The current quick and heavy plans select the same ordered 122 and 243 steps. The completed tests cover the full current selection.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 122 steps passed. The first run passed 80 steps and had 42 build failures from stale seeded kernel and geometry metadata. After a targeted cache clean, all 42 failed steps passed with `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1`. No source change was needed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 243 steps passed, 0 failed, in 44.8 minutes. The gate checked the declared known failures at their expected assertions.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed in 2 minutes 29 seconds.\n- `app suites: example_catalog` ran in the quick gate: 37 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored. All four ignored catalog tests passed in the heavy gate.\n- `app suites: solid_law_goldens` ran in the quick gate: 7 passed, 0 failed.\n- `meridian::tests::tool_meridian_checks_inputs_before_shape_fallbacks` pins named errors for malformed tool dimensions.\n- `meridian::tests::accepted_extreme_meridians_have_finite_correct_radii` pins finite, correct interpolation for accepted extreme inputs.\n- `meridian::tests::meridian_refuses_overflowing_lengths_and_circle_ranges` pins named refusals for unsupported segment lengths and circle coordinates.\n- Mutation proof: removing the input guard made `tool_meridian_checks_inputs_before_shape_fallbacks` fail on the NaN drill. Restoring the guard made it pass.\n- Mutation proof: restoring the old interpolation made `accepted_extreme_meridians_have_finite_correct_radii` fail on a non-finite radius. Restoring the fix made it pass.\n- Mutation proof: removing the length guard and circle bounds separately made `meridian_refuses_overflowing_lengths_and_circle_ranges` fail. Each mutation returned `Ok` instead of `OutOfRange`. Each restored check passed.\n- All four mutations failed with exit 101. Each restored pin passed with exit 0. All seven meridian tests passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The catalog and solid-law golden suites passed. The diff changes no catalog entry or recorded program.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No consumer reads the meridian, so no end-to-end path runs through it.\n- No real router bit record (roundover, cove) exists yet. The concave-arc tests use a hand-built roundover meridian.\n\nNo UI file changes. UI screenshots do not apply.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes these files.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/3367-tool-meridian.md`.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: Tools: a tool meridian (lines and arcs) for each mill kind, split into convex atoms with outer and inner bounds for concave arcs (internal; no output change).\n\nFixes #3367\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
